WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.080
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:07.080
Politics is a strange thing; it can switch
in an instant from dullness to disaster, from

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.740
inspiring to insanity, and from dinner table
chat to fighting in the street.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.690
And much of the problem with it is that when
you align yourself with one particular group,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:22.100
you feel obliged to stick up for them, for
better or for worse, leading to arguments.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.300
So what about the few politicians that we
can agree on?

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.410
Seem like an impossible task, doesn’t it,
surely such a rare creature doesn’t exist

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:32.410
in the wild.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:37.780
Well, you’re in for a big surprise, because
here’s five politicians that everyone will

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.660
love.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:45.750
First we head to Canada but not for the lustrous
hair of Justin Trudeau.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:52.120
The Rhinoceros party was set up in 1963 by
Jacques Ferron, a physician and author.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.850
It was intended as political satire, and it
kept going for 30 years.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:02.820
In a refreshing display of honesty, their
creed was a promise to keep none of their

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:03.820
promises.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:08.790
They listed their leader as an actual rhinoceros
from a Montreal zoo, called Cornelius the

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.330
first, since you need a thick skin to be a
leader.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:17.580
Members also claimed to be Marxists-Leninists
but rather than having any communist ideals,

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:22.050
it was just because they were fans of Groucho
Marx and John Lennon.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:26.030
Over the years, some of the party’s policies
included:

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:31.910
• Changing Canada's currency to bubble gum,
so it could be inflated or deflated at will.

00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:34.860
• Repealing the law of gravity.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.990
• Providing higher education by building
taller schools.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:44.409
Although they never won a single seat, they
did occasionally embarrass authentic political

00:01:44.409 --> 00:01:49.810
parties, such as when Sonia, a professional
clown, came in second for one of the seats

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.400
in 1980.

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:56.920
The party was forced to disband in 1993 due
to a change in the law that would force them

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:03.390
to run for at least 50 seats, at a cost of
$1,000 a seat, that’s far too pricey for

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.760
a good old political jest.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:10.509
In the same year that the Rhinoceros Party
was founded, a similarly satirical approach

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:14.660
was being adopted in the UK by rock singer
David Sutch.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:21.780
In 1963, he represented a range of different
made up parties in the parliamentary elections,

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:27.250
most notably the National Teenage Party since,
at that time, the voting age was 21, which

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.490
Sutch disagreed with.

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:34.150
His band, Screaming Lord Sutch and the Savages,
were not especially successful but their line-up

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:39.620
was constantly changing and they had many
of rock’s superstars before they were famous,

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:45.040
including Jimmy Page of Led Zeppelin, Ritchie
Blackmore of Deep Purple, and Noel Redding,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.970
who was Jimi Hendrix’s bass player.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:52.580
Sutch returned to politics in the 80s, after
leaving America when he was shot during a

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.990
mugging, a fairly solid sign that you don’t
belong somewhere.

00:02:55.990 --> 00:03:02.209
He set up the now infamous Monster Raving
Loony Party and was joined by others including

00:03:02.209 --> 00:03:08.460
a retired WWII hero named Bill Boaks, who
had been part of the sinking of the Bismark.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.680
Although they never won any seats in parliament,
they did take a number of council spots in

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:17.330
Devon where they spent a lot of time trying
to annoy the Conservatives, with one Loony

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.910
Party councilor attempting to pay some taxes
with a pile of metal.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.560
But across the country, they established themselves
as one of the leading protest vote groups

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.050
for many years.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:35.209
Sutch sadly commited suicide in 1999 but,
as was fitting for his party, they elected

00:03:35.209 --> 00:03:40.530
Alan "Howling Laud" Hope and his cat, Catmando,
to take over the leadership.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:46.030
The party’s policies include, putting a
massive mirror in the sky to reflect the sunlight

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:52.050
during the nighttime, so solar panels still
work; introducing a 99 pence coin, to make

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:57.600
it easier to buy ice cream; and bungee cords
shall be attached to the rear of all cars

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.450
so that no fuel is used on the return journey.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:07.260
When Donald Trump announced that Linda McMahon,
the co-founder of wrestling franchise WWE,

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:13.300
would be a part of his new government, a group
of Mexicans deserved credit for their groundbreaking

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:16.039
work 20 years earlier.

00:04:16.039 --> 00:04:21.969
In 1996, a wrestler named Superbarrio ran
for President of the United States and arranged

00:04:21.969 --> 00:04:27.130
rallies on both sides of the Mexican border,
promising to do away with border patrols and

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:29.439
the Drug Enforcement Agency.

00:04:29.439 --> 00:04:35.009
Although he dressed in a red and yellow Lucha
wrestling outfit, Superbarrio was a true political

00:04:35.009 --> 00:04:37.840
activist, rather than a comedy figure.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:43.639
Unfortunately, his attempts to wrestle his
way into the political ranks were unsuccessful.

00:04:43.639 --> 00:04:49.210
Dick Augustsson is a Swedish IT entrepreneur
who, when he grew tired of endless jokes about

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:54.969
his first name, decided to change the whole
thing and become Rick Falkvinge, or Falconwing,

00:04:54.969 --> 00:04:56.710
as it’s translated.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.520
Through his love of technology, he was part
of the early file sharing communities so,

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:06.879
when the internet copyright debate began to
pick up internationally in 2005, he decided

00:05:06.879 --> 00:05:10.520
to get involved by setting up the Pirate Party.

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.949
His domain got 3 million hits in the first
two days.

00:05:13.949 --> 00:05:18.910
But he wasn’t just casually dipping a toe
in to politics; he quit his job, took out

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:24.080
a large bank loan and really put his heart
and soul into the party.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:29.580
Within a year, he made the international news,
as a voice criticizing the raid on The Pirate

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:34.460
Bay, a famous file-sharing site based in Sweden,
don’t know why I’m telling you that, you

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:35.849
know what The Pirate Bay is.

00:05:35.849 --> 00:05:42.289
He only managed 0.63% of the vote in 2006
but by the time the European Elections came

00:05:42.289 --> 00:05:49.849
around in 2009, he won the massive majority
of the youth vote, taking 25% of those under

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:52.770
30 and over 7% overall.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:57.409
He’s been recognized around the world as
a key figure in bringing the internet into

00:05:57.409 --> 00:06:01.999
politics, well before we started electing
people on the basis of emails and twitter…

00:06:01.999 --> 00:06:03.619
ah, the good old days.

00:06:03.619 --> 00:06:09.180
If you are going to elect a bad-tempered ape
with no idea what it’s doing, Brazil at

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.249
least decided to go for an actual chimpanzee.

00:06:12.249 --> 00:06:18.899
Tiao the Chimp was estimated to have received
a massive 400,000 votes in the 1988 election

00:06:18.899 --> 00:06:21.259
for mayor of Rio De Janeiro.

00:06:21.259 --> 00:06:28.719
He came third out of twelve candidates, or
to put it another way, nine actual human politicians

00:06:28.719 --> 00:06:30.939
were beaten by a monkey.

00:06:30.939 --> 00:06:37.490
The Chimp eventually died of diabetes because,
as the saying goes in Brazil; with great power

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:44.900
comes great amounts of churros.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:54.669
Thanks for watching.

